<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.HtmlBridge.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.8.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.5.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.5.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Scripting is the top of the Broiler.JS side of this component and reaches Dom, Core,
    DomBridgeUtils, Jseal and Jseal.BroilerJs transitively, so one reference is the whole
    default closure. The suite tests internals of several of those; each grants
    InternalsVisibleTo to this assembly by name.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Broiler.HtmlBridge.Scripting\Broiler.HtmlBridge.Scripting.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    THE VM SIDE IS CONDITIONAL, AND THE CONDITION IS THE POINT.

    VmScriptEngineTests names the VM script engine, so an unconditional reference would drag
    the five Broiler.VM projects into every build of this suite — precisely the coupling the
    two configurations exist to keep optional. That file guards ITSELF with
    `#if BROILER_VM_JS`, the constant eng/Broiler.Configurations.props defines from
    $(BroilerJavaScriptEngine), so it needs no item here.

    Jseal/VmProviderRegistration.cs cannot use that trick: it exists to NAME the provider
    assembly so the CLR loads it and its module initializer runs, and a file emptied by a
    preprocessor guard would still leave a reference-less build trying to resolve the item.
    It is conditioned as an item instead.

    The conformance suite itself names no engine type — that is what makes it a conformance
    suite — so it cannot be the thing that registers a provider. Registration happens here,
    in the assembly that already knows which configuration it is.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(BroilerJavaScriptEngine)' == 'Vm'">
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Broiler.HtmlBridge.Scripting.Vm\Broiler.HtmlBridge.Scripting.Vm.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="Jseal\VmProviderRegistration.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(BroilerJavaScriptEngine)' == 'Vm'">
    <Compile Include="Jseal\VmProviderRegistration.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
